The Debug.Assert statements are used to validate the state of the program before it performs a certain operation. If the condition is not true, the program will terminate and throw an exception. 

Please note that Debug.Assert requires a DEBUG configuration for its assertions to work. If you want to use these assertions in non-DEBUG configurations, you should use the System.Diagnostics.Contracts namespace.
